WEBVTT

00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:11.440
<i>Witnesses are disappearing one after another.</i>

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:15.390
<i>Could there be a modern-day Jack the Ripper?</i>

00:00:15.390 --> 00:00:17.890
We're leaving now.

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:19.950
See you tonight.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:23.710
Still can't forget about that girl?

00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:27.000
That incident was resolved two hours ago.

00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:30.210
And you've been deep in thought 
for two hours since then.

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:35.010
I'm just tired.

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:36.550
I'm going to sleep.

00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:38.890
Can't you change in the changing room?

00:00:38.890 --> 00:00:41.520
You're such a lazy count.

00:00:48.650 --> 00:00:49.710
It's an emergency!

00:00:49.710 --> 00:00:51.780
Something unbelievable has happened!

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:57.280
Isn't there something you should 
say before you start screaming?

00:00:57.820 --> 00:01:00.530
My friend Shinyao was kidnapped!

00:01:03.590 --> 00:01:06.000
That certainly is an emergency.

00:02:37.460 --> 00:02:41.720
<b>Episode 2 Shadows Who Fight Shadows</b>

00:02:39.640 --> 00:02:43.390
Seems like what she said was true.

00:02:43.860 --> 00:02:46.120
We're going to check out the area.

00:02:46.120 --> 00:02:48.260
I'll let you know if we figure anything out.

00:02:48.260 --> 00:02:48.930
Got it.

00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:50.130
Thanks.

00:02:55.250 --> 00:02:56.280
I'm going with them.

00:02:56.510 --> 00:02:57.550
Calm down.

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:03.020
Ow...

00:03:05.030 --> 00:03:06.910
I told you to calm down.

00:03:07.370 --> 00:03:09.110
Why can't I leave?

00:03:09.110 --> 00:03:11.870
I passed through easily when I came in.

00:03:11.870 --> 00:03:14.810
This is a special seating area.

00:03:14.810 --> 00:03:16.380
It has all kinds of enchantments on it.

00:03:16.990 --> 00:03:18.450
Really?

00:03:19.150 --> 00:03:21.660
Let Luke and Toryu handle the search.

00:03:21.660 --> 00:03:23.550
They're far more useful than you are.

00:03:24.390 --> 00:03:27.660
Now, why don't you tell me

00:03:27.660 --> 00:03:30.430
how you were able to remember me?

00:03:30.430 --> 00:03:32.770
How? I...

00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:38.860
You put your face really 
close to mine, and...

00:03:41.610 --> 00:03:43.700
You don't know?

00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:46.870
Then perhaps it's a 
property of Rijan's blood.

00:03:46.870 --> 00:03:50.610
Or maybe the shock of your friend's 
kidnapping broke the spell.

00:03:50.610 --> 00:03:53.250
Spell? So you did do something to—

00:03:53.250 --> 00:03:55.580
It doesn't matter anymore.

00:03:55.930 --> 00:03:58.800
More importantly, give me all the 
information you have on your friend.

00:03:59.330 --> 00:04:01.570
All the visual and audio data you have.

00:04:01.570 --> 00:04:03.760
Anything that could serve as a clue.

00:04:03.970 --> 00:04:06.070
<i>He's definitely trying to distract me.</i>

00:04:06.580 --> 00:04:08.430
<i>It's infuriating.</i>

00:04:11.850 --> 00:04:13.490
And this is really good.

00:04:13.490 --> 00:04:15.230
How even more infuriating.

00:04:27.080 --> 00:04:28.800
Let's make this quick.

00:04:28.800 --> 00:04:30.620
The others will suspect something.

00:04:30.620 --> 00:04:32.960
Thanks for meeting us, Detective Gregory.

00:04:33.160 --> 00:04:36.420
Your nose is as keen as ever, wolfman.

00:04:36.810 --> 00:04:38.490
Which means I'm right.

00:04:38.490 --> 00:04:39.250
Yeah.

00:04:39.540 --> 00:04:41.610
This isn't the work of a human.

00:04:41.610 --> 00:04:43.970
They broke in through the window,

00:04:44.170 --> 00:04:46.760
kidnapped the victim, and escaped 
back out through the window.

00:04:47.100 --> 00:04:51.100
According to her roommate, 
it only took a few seconds.

00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:54.070
I'm pretty sure that's what she said.

00:04:54.730 --> 00:04:56.760
And we're on the fourth floor.

00:04:56.760 --> 00:04:59.690
If it was a human, how did they do it?

00:05:00.150 --> 00:05:03.120
Should we investigate pole 
vault gold medalists?

00:05:05.320 --> 00:05:05.950
Luke.

00:05:06.340 --> 00:05:08.160
It's nothing.

00:05:08.350 --> 00:05:10.370
Those are scratches.

00:05:10.370 --> 00:05:12.870
I can't report this to my superiors.

00:05:15.730 --> 00:05:18.540
Is he one of yours, wolfman?

00:05:19.030 --> 00:05:21.590
That's not funny, officer.

00:05:21.590 --> 00:05:27.500
Either way, it seems a bit 
strange for the work of a Shadow.

00:05:27.500 --> 00:05:28.800
Strange how?

00:05:29.090 --> 00:05:32.640
Yeah. Why did they act in the middle 
of the day if they're a Shadow?

00:05:33.240 --> 00:05:36.260
Why did they go after a foreign 
student who just arrived in London?

00:05:36.260 --> 00:05:38.620
Was the victim special somehow?

00:05:41.620 --> 00:05:44.070
It wasn't a goblin or spriggan.

00:05:44.070 --> 00:05:46.370
They're not that smart.

00:05:46.370 --> 00:05:49.620
Maybe there's a mastermind controlling them,

00:05:49.900 --> 00:05:52.210
and they're out for revenge?

00:05:52.210 --> 00:05:56.290
Or maybe the commotion caused 
by the goblins made them notice.

00:05:56.470 --> 00:05:57.920
Notice what?

00:05:58.170 --> 00:05:58.890
That—

00:05:58.890 --> 00:06:02.960
<i>That you've arrived in London.</i>

00:06:03.120 --> 00:06:03.880
What?

00:06:03.880 --> 00:06:06.420
Wayne, stay out of this.

00:06:06.420 --> 00:06:10.150
<i>But I don't think hiding 
it from her will help.</i>

00:06:10.150 --> 00:06:11.550
You mean...

00:06:11.550 --> 00:06:14.820
<i>Hey, miss. Your great-grandmother—</i>

00:06:15.790 --> 00:06:17.770
Who was that? What did they mean?

00:06:17.950 --> 00:06:19.010
Who knows?

00:06:19.010 --> 00:06:21.090
Probably just a passerby talking to himself.

00:06:21.090 --> 00:06:23.480
You think I'd believe that?

00:06:23.780 --> 00:06:26.650
That boy was definitely talking to me.

00:06:26.650 --> 00:06:28.570
They mentioned my great-grandmother.

00:06:28.990 --> 00:06:30.240
Because...

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:32.120
<i>You're so mean, Vlad.</i>

00:06:34.630 --> 00:06:37.960
<i>I woke up so I could help you guys.</i>

00:06:38.210 --> 00:06:40.420
What's going on? The radio 
turned on by itself.

00:06:40.420 --> 00:06:41.830
<i>Nice to meet you, miss.</i>

00:06:42.020 --> 00:06:43.310
<i>I'm Wayne.</i>

00:06:43.310 --> 00:06:45.590
<i>I'm the ghost that haunts this place.</i>

00:06:48.680 --> 00:06:52.580
You probably realized after 
yesterday's incident,

00:06:52.580 --> 00:06:55.220
but there are non-human 
entities in this world.

00:06:57.730 --> 00:06:59.560
Including you?

00:06:59.560 --> 00:07:02.530
<i>We're called Umbra.</i>

00:07:02.530 --> 00:07:05.610
<i>Some people call us Shadows.</i>

00:07:06.110 --> 00:07:07.070
Umbra?

00:07:07.070 --> 00:07:09.050
<i>Yeah. Umbra are—</i>

00:07:09.050 --> 00:07:12.780
We're born from human fear and anxiety.

00:07:13.110 --> 00:07:15.770
As a child, when you woke 
up during the night,

00:07:15.770 --> 00:07:20.620
did you ever imagine demons or 
monsters in the shadows of your room?

00:07:21.920 --> 00:07:27.610
In those moments, the monsters you 
imagined were there beyond the darkness.

00:07:28.650 --> 00:07:31.840
Rather, you could say you created them.

00:07:32.280 --> 00:07:34.050
What are you talking about?

00:07:34.220 --> 00:07:36.010
<i>Strange, isn't it?</i>

00:07:36.010 --> 00:07:37.640
<i>You're not scared because they're there.</i>

00:07:37.640 --> 00:07:40.790
<i>They're there because 
you're scared. It's like—</i>

00:07:42.470 --> 00:07:47.810
Luke is a descendant of the werewolves 
you've heard about in fairy tales.

00:07:47.810 --> 00:07:51.120
Though currently he's a lone wolf 
who's broken away from the pack.

00:07:51.810 --> 00:07:55.300
Toryu is a jiangshi of 
your country's traditions.

00:07:55.300 --> 00:08:00.170
After coming to life there, 
he accompanied Rijan here.

00:08:01.100 --> 00:08:02.650
My great-grandmother?

00:08:02.650 --> 00:08:03.830
Then he...

00:08:07.250 --> 00:08:10.300
I heard he's been around 
since the 19th century.

00:08:10.860 --> 00:08:12.530
<i>I'm younger than that.</i>

00:08:12.530 --> 00:08:16.050
<i>Though, actually, I don't remember 
the specifics of how I was born.</i>

00:08:16.600 --> 00:08:18.010
You don't remember?

00:08:18.370 --> 00:08:21.200
His memory and existence are hazy.

00:08:21.200 --> 00:08:22.980
It's the reason he doesn't have a body.

00:08:23.180 --> 00:08:25.960
<i>Six months ago, Vlad picked me up</i>

00:08:25.960 --> 00:08:28.370
<i>while I was just a consciousness 
inside an abandoned doll...</i>

00:08:29.780 --> 00:08:31.360
So, what are you?

00:08:31.610 --> 00:08:32.560
Me?

00:08:33.350 --> 00:08:36.570
To be perfectly honest, I am a proud—

00:08:37.420 --> 00:08:38.660
Excuse me.

00:08:41.830 --> 00:08:43.460
<b>Mu Shinyao</b>

00:08:42.300 --> 00:08:43.460
Shinyao?

00:08:43.680 --> 00:08:46.040
Wait. Isn't your friend's phone...

00:08:46.770 --> 00:08:48.380
The police took it.

00:08:48.570 --> 00:08:50.320
Shinyao? Shinyao!

00:08:50.320 --> 00:08:51.590
<i>Baileu Ton-sama.</i>

00:08:52.380 --> 00:08:56.500
<i>It's possible something has 
happened to Mu Shinyao-sama.</i>

00:08:56.500 --> 00:08:59.720
<i>Please confirm Shinyao-sama's 
location immediately.</i>

00:09:02.300 --> 00:09:04.180
<i>What is it? What happened?</i>

00:09:12.950 --> 00:09:13.850
Haysin.

00:09:14.430 --> 00:09:17.410
Chris-kun, huh? You're right on time.

00:09:17.680 --> 00:09:20.370
You're going to eat all of that yourself?

00:09:20.890 --> 00:09:23.620
You've got a lot of energy 
for such an old man.

00:09:24.270 --> 00:09:27.790
Maintaining this body is a lot of work.

00:09:27.790 --> 00:09:29.040
How did it go?

00:09:29.360 --> 00:09:32.420
I took the package to 
the designated location.

00:09:32.620 --> 00:09:34.340
She should be waking up soon.

00:09:34.750 --> 00:09:36.920
Sorry about the short notice.

00:09:36.920 --> 00:09:38.140
You did well.

00:09:38.310 --> 00:09:39.630
Don't worry about that.

00:09:39.630 --> 00:09:42.970
Just make this the last 
disgusting job I do for you.

00:09:43.410 --> 00:09:45.640
Did it not suit your style?

00:09:46.060 --> 00:09:49.970
I thought your organization 
was created to help people.

00:09:49.970 --> 00:09:51.520
Why are you kidnapping them?

00:09:51.800 --> 00:09:55.560
Sometimes you have to use 
people to help people.

00:09:55.560 --> 00:09:57.490
It's not that unusual.

00:09:57.700 --> 00:10:00.200
What's going to happen to her now?

00:10:00.200 --> 00:10:05.410
She's bait to awaken Rijan's blood relative.

00:10:05.610 --> 00:10:06.810
What does that mean?

00:10:10.340 --> 00:10:12.750
You're going to hand her over to that filth?

00:10:26.400 --> 00:10:27.310
Huh?

00:10:28.150 --> 00:10:29.020
Where am I?

00:10:37.500 --> 00:10:40.810
Huh? Wasn't this mannequin just...

00:10:41.240 --> 00:10:42.180
What?!

00:10:58.930 --> 00:11:00.800
You can come in.

00:11:06.120 --> 00:11:07.620
Thanks for inviting me.

00:11:07.620 --> 00:11:09.860
You've got a convenient power.

00:11:09.860 --> 00:11:11.270
Did you even need me?

00:11:11.500 --> 00:11:16.630
I can't actually enter buildings 
unless I'm invited in.

00:11:16.630 --> 00:11:19.810
Your traditions are 
surprisingly inconvenient.

00:11:19.810 --> 00:11:20.860
Here.

00:11:21.020 --> 00:11:23.070
This is the victim's phone.

00:11:25.040 --> 00:11:27.180
I'll be borrowing this for a while.

00:11:29.700 --> 00:11:31.790
Return it by dawn.

00:11:33.450 --> 00:11:34.540
That jerk!

00:11:34.540 --> 00:11:36.320
He left me!

00:11:39.270 --> 00:11:41.840
I don't know much about Umbra or Shadows,

00:11:41.840 --> 00:11:45.130
but judging by this room 
he's just a shut-in.

00:11:45.130 --> 00:11:49.060
Aw, jeez! Maybe I'll go look for her myself.

00:11:49.600 --> 00:11:52.400
But he's right. I just arrived in London.

00:11:52.400 --> 00:11:54.820
Even if I search at random...

00:11:54.820 --> 00:11:56.350
Aw, jeez!

00:11:56.980 --> 00:11:58.690
Huh? What's this?

00:11:59.070 --> 00:12:01.400
This huge thing's in the middle of the room.

00:12:01.560 --> 00:12:03.910
Wait, what?

00:12:08.350 --> 00:12:13.390
There's data of the kidnapping 
on Shinyao's phone?

00:12:13.390 --> 00:12:15.710
It's just a possibility.

00:12:16.000 --> 00:12:17.420
So, what's the password?

00:12:17.770 --> 00:12:18.830
Who knows?

00:12:18.830 --> 00:12:20.730
Wayne, wake up. You're up.

00:12:20.730 --> 00:12:21.630
<i>Got it.</i>

00:12:21.850 --> 00:12:23.340
<i>Give me a minute.</i>

00:12:23.710 --> 00:12:24.860
He's there.

00:12:25.660 --> 00:12:28.360
<i>I'm here. Let's get started.</i>

00:12:33.820 --> 00:12:35.350
<i>I got in!</i>

00:12:35.540 --> 00:12:39.070
Wayne, you'd better stay off my phone!

00:12:39.340 --> 00:12:41.480
It's an app called "Magic Mirror."

00:12:41.480 --> 00:12:42.690
Investigate it.

00:12:42.690 --> 00:12:45.700
Sounds like something 
an evil witch would use.

00:12:45.700 --> 00:12:47.450
<i>Don't you know, Luke?</i>

00:12:47.450 --> 00:12:51.910
<i>It's a super popular app with over a 
hundred million users around the world.</i>

00:12:51.910 --> 00:12:55.180
One that gives you directions, 
looks up information,

00:12:55.180 --> 00:12:57.380
and does whatever else you 
want if you talk to it?

00:12:57.380 --> 00:13:01.080
<i>That's how conversation 
apps have worked until now.</i>

00:13:01.080 --> 00:13:04.300
<i>But this one predicts your thoughts.</i>

00:13:04.520 --> 00:13:05.730
What do you mean?

00:13:05.730 --> 00:13:07.510
<i>Even if you don't ask,</i>

00:13:07.510 --> 00:13:10.570
<i>it'll examine your usage,
 conversation history,</i>

00:13:10.570 --> 00:13:14.060
<i>expressions, and breathing to give you advice.</i>

00:13:15.260 --> 00:13:16.920
Do you get what he's talking about?

00:13:18.160 --> 00:13:19.060
<i>In other words,</i>

00:13:19.500 --> 00:13:24.820
<i>it makes full use of the phone's 
functionality to read the user's thoughts.</i>

00:13:25.310 --> 00:13:29.240
<i>They say it can read about 
80% of your thoughts.</i>

00:13:29.240 --> 00:13:30.990
That's creepy.

00:13:30.990 --> 00:13:33.470
Maybe it can read thoughts,

00:13:33.470 --> 00:13:38.920
but can it sense when its user 
is in danger and seeks help?

00:13:38.920 --> 00:13:43.380
<i>If it's true, that would make 
this a rather high-level AI.</i>

00:13:43.690 --> 00:13:45.580
Talk about a busybody.

00:13:45.580 --> 00:13:46.840
What is it, your mom?

00:13:46.840 --> 00:13:47.970
<i>I found it.</i>

00:13:48.280 --> 00:13:52.370
<i>Magic Mirror contacted 
the girl's phone, and...</i>

00:13:52.370 --> 00:13:52.930
<i>Huh?</i>

00:13:53.160 --> 00:13:54.100
What's up?

00:13:54.350 --> 00:13:57.560
<i>They're on the phone right now.</i>

00:13:58.390 --> 00:13:59.290
What?

00:14:01.880 --> 00:14:03.320
Shinyao, run!

00:14:03.700 --> 00:14:06.280
Mirror, mirror. Tell me where Shinyao is.

00:14:06.520 --> 00:14:07.740
<i>Roger that.</i>

00:14:07.740 --> 00:14:09.490
<i>I'll show you a map of your destination.</i>

00:14:10.380 --> 00:14:11.940
Show me how to get there.

00:14:11.940 --> 00:14:13.580
<i>Make your way to the 
major thoroughfare first.</i>

00:14:13.920 --> 00:14:15.420
<i>Take the next left.</i>

00:14:15.420 --> 00:14:16.540
Thanks.

00:14:16.870 --> 00:14:18.250
What's going on?

00:14:18.580 --> 00:14:21.010
Wayne, how are you getting that video?

00:14:21.010 --> 00:14:22.360
<i>It's not me.</i>

00:14:22.360 --> 00:14:25.460
<i>The app is sending her the video.</i>

00:14:25.970 --> 00:14:29.040
Looks like some security camera footage.

00:14:29.040 --> 00:14:30.300
In other words,

00:14:30.500 --> 00:14:36.270
she's being shown a video of 
her friend in mortal danger.

00:14:36.270 --> 00:14:38.440
Hold on. If she sees this...

00:14:38.730 --> 00:14:41.150
Yeah, we're talking about that tomboy.

00:14:41.150 --> 00:14:43.260
She's probably already on her way there.

00:14:43.260 --> 00:14:44.180
Ton-sama.

00:14:44.180 --> 00:14:46.030
But what's the meaning of this?

00:14:46.030 --> 00:14:48.490
Why is the app doing this on its own?

00:14:48.490 --> 00:14:51.740
<i>Probably because she wanted the information.</i>

00:14:51.930 --> 00:14:55.950
If its navigational system takes her there, 
it's more malicious than considerate.

00:14:55.950 --> 00:14:59.290
<i>Maybe it really is malicious.</i>

00:14:59.480 --> 00:15:01.900
You think it's the work of an Umbra?

00:15:01.900 --> 00:15:05.080
<i>An Umbra like me who doesn't have 
a physical body could do it.</i>

00:15:05.620 --> 00:15:06.510
Could it be?

00:15:07.660 --> 00:15:08.260
Wait.

00:15:08.580 --> 00:15:11.970
Even if we go after her now, 
we won't make it in time.

00:15:11.970 --> 00:15:13.760
Our enemies will have accounted for that.

00:15:13.760 --> 00:15:14.310
But...

00:15:14.310 --> 00:15:15.970
You're just going to abandon her, Vlad?

00:15:15.970 --> 00:15:17.570
Haven't you—

00:15:17.570 --> 00:15:20.580
So we'll go after her faster 
than they're expecting.

00:15:20.580 --> 00:15:21.630
Huh?

00:15:21.630 --> 00:15:22.270
Wayne.

00:15:22.270 --> 00:15:23.310
<i>What?</i>

00:15:23.660 --> 00:15:25.430
Connect me to her phone.

00:15:37.220 --> 00:15:38.330
This is it, right?

00:15:40.090 --> 00:15:41.420
Shinyao!

00:15:41.720 --> 00:15:43.630
Shinyao!

00:15:44.840 --> 00:15:45.980
Shinyao?

00:15:45.980 --> 00:15:47.700
<i>Get out of there!</i>

00:15:48.140 --> 00:15:48.960
Wayne?

00:15:48.960 --> 00:15:51.030
<i>Can't you tell? It's a trap!</i>

00:15:51.030 --> 00:15:53.120
<i>Their real goal is—</i>

00:16:05.840 --> 00:16:06.870
Shinyao!

00:16:09.010 --> 00:16:10.360
<i>Huh? Hey...</i>

00:16:10.360 --> 00:16:13.360
<i>Hey! Don't leave me!</i>

00:16:23.900 --> 00:16:25.790
Shinyao!

00:16:25.790 --> 00:16:27.790
Shinyao, run!

00:16:31.480 --> 00:16:32.550
Ton?

00:16:45.590 --> 00:16:47.160
You have to run.

00:16:47.590 --> 00:16:49.870
Whatever you do, don't come this way.

00:16:53.670 --> 00:16:54.560
Ton...

00:16:57.080 --> 00:16:57.920
Who's there?

00:17:09.670 --> 00:17:10.380
Come on!

00:17:10.380 --> 00:17:12.070
Over here, slasher!

00:17:15.870 --> 00:17:18.480
It's okay. Shinyao and I
 will make it out okay.

00:17:18.480 --> 00:17:21.800
Our college life in London is waiting for us.

00:17:28.010 --> 00:17:29.040
No way...

00:17:35.340 --> 00:17:36.570
I made it in time.

00:17:36.930 --> 00:17:38.010
Great.

00:17:38.430 --> 00:17:40.160
Wh-Who...

00:17:41.490 --> 00:17:42.390
are you?

00:17:42.390 --> 00:17:44.580
I'm Wayne. You're so mean.

00:17:44.580 --> 00:17:45.940
Huh? What?

00:17:45.940 --> 00:17:47.090
But that body...

00:17:47.090 --> 00:17:48.630
Oh, this is...

00:17:51.110 --> 00:17:51.920
Ow!

00:17:52.220 --> 00:17:54.550
It's a mannequin.

00:17:54.870 --> 00:17:56.870
Don't put too much strain on it.

00:17:56.870 --> 00:17:58.150
Too late!

00:18:06.480 --> 00:18:07.390
Huh?

00:18:07.390 --> 00:18:08.520
Miss!

00:18:16.030 --> 00:18:17.530
<i>Call me.</i>

00:18:17.530 --> 00:18:19.510
Vlad? What do you mean?

00:18:19.510 --> 00:18:20.740
<i>Just call me.</i>

00:18:21.000 --> 00:18:24.270
Stop speaking nonsense and help me!

00:18:26.290 --> 00:18:27.670
<i>Got it.</i>

00:18:40.430 --> 00:18:41.520
Well done, Wayne.

00:18:41.520 --> 00:18:43.100
You're late, Vlad.

00:18:45.100 --> 00:18:46.980
Why are you so reckless?

00:18:47.540 --> 00:18:51.390
Why are you so much like Rijan?

00:18:51.390 --> 00:18:52.230
What?

00:18:53.440 --> 00:18:54.310
Vlad!

00:18:55.110 --> 00:18:58.290
Sorry to have kept you waiting,
 you degenerate!

00:18:58.940 --> 00:19:04.640
Rather, Jack the Ripper, the serial killer
 who once terrorized London.

00:19:06.350 --> 00:19:11.480
I wish I could admonish you 
for your twisted aesthetic,

00:19:11.480 --> 00:19:13.440
but unfortunately there's no time.

00:19:13.440 --> 00:19:15.930
It's time to say goodbye, killer.

00:19:16.690 --> 00:19:19.390
Just so you know, my name is—

00:19:19.390 --> 00:19:20.480
Vampire.

00:19:21.090 --> 00:19:23.500
Actually, it's Count Dracula.

00:19:23.500 --> 00:19:25.390
Bram Stoker's exquisitely-crafted

00:19:25.390 --> 00:19:27.850
ultimate vampire.

00:19:30.910 --> 00:19:31.750
Come!

00:20:09.360 --> 00:20:13.440
No one said you could kill the other girl.

00:20:15.810 --> 00:20:20.650
I suppose you were filth the 
moment you tried to kill a woman.

00:20:38.180 --> 00:20:40.550
Sorry for scaring you,

00:20:43.280 --> 00:20:44.700
but don't worry.

00:20:44.700 --> 00:20:47.350
I swear I'll protect you now.

00:22:20.910 --> 00:22:23.020
This was Vlad, wasn't it?

00:22:23.020 --> 00:22:25.740
Yeah, he really put on a show.

00:22:30.530 --> 00:22:33.670
<i>Is he one of yours, wolfman?</i>

00:22:35.290 --> 00:23:32.140
<b>Phantom Twilight 
Plus</b>

00:22:36.100 --> 00:22:37.820
Phantom in the Twilight Plus!

00:22:38.800 --> 00:22:44.470
In this episode we'll introduce the 
unreliable leader of us Twilights.

00:22:44.790 --> 00:22:46.200
Vlad Garfunkel.

00:22:46.200 --> 00:22:48.430
I'm a vampire descended from Count Dracula.

00:22:48.430 --> 00:22:51.140
But that aside, what do 
you mean by unreliable?

00:22:51.540 --> 00:22:56.840
You just barely introduced yourself at the 
very end, but it was obvious from the start.

00:22:56.840 --> 00:22:58.420
You wasted your time.

00:22:58.420 --> 00:23:00.210
What a sloppy introduction!

00:23:00.210 --> 00:23:05.140
Since he's a vampire, sunlight, 
garlic, crosses, running water...

00:23:05.140 --> 00:23:06.820
He's got a whole host of weaknesses.

00:23:06.820 --> 00:23:08.700
What a useless leader.

00:23:08.700 --> 00:23:10.590
I just don't like them. I'm fine.

00:23:10.590 --> 00:23:12.160
Are you trying to pick a fight, Luke?

00:23:12.160 --> 00:23:14.460
Naturally, his special 
ability is sucking blood.

00:23:14.460 --> 00:23:17.230
If he sucks your blood, 
you'll turn into an Umbra.

00:23:17.230 --> 00:23:20.000
Watch out, especially you 
young girls out there.

00:23:20.000 --> 00:23:23.650
Don't worry. I haven't sucked 
anyone's blood in a hundred years.

00:23:23.650 --> 00:23:27.880
Not since I met Rijan and 
joined the Twilights...

00:23:27.880 --> 00:23:32.970
This useless coward can't 
forget the girl from his past.

00:23:32.970 --> 00:23:34.490
We appreciate your continued support.

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:50.050
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:35.330 --> 00:23:36.950
The search for Shinyao continues.

00:23:36.950 --> 00:23:39.590
Ton feels responsible and becomes despondent, 
while Luke kindly comforts her.

00:23:39.590 --> 00:23:41.400
However, behind the scenes 
he destroys evidence,

00:23:41.400 --> 00:23:43.760
acts alone, and is otherwise 
highly suspicious.

00:23:43.760 --> 00:23:45.690
Hey, Luke. Be honest.

00:23:45.690 --> 00:23:47.560
You know who's behind this, don't you?

00:23:46.980 --> 00:23:50.050
<b>
Episode 3 Twisted Bond</b>

00:23:47.560 --> 00:23:49.630
Next time: Twisted Bond.
